\begin_layout Subsubsection
System Architecture
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Sender:
 Raspberry Pi Pico W;
 receiver Max/MSP (via Python);
 communication:
 UDP + OSC payload.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Packet Structure
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The packet consisted of a header (12 bytes) which had a version number,
 device ID,
 sequence number and payload length.
 Then comes the OSC payload itself.
 Finally there is an authentication tag (truncated HMAC).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Authentication Mechanism
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This is HMAC-SHA256 over (header || OSC payload).
 This is truncated to 16 bytes.
 The key is NOT transmitted and is shared out of bands (?)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Replay Protection
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Monotonically increasing sequence numbers.
 Receiver rejects duplicates or out-of-order packets (depending on policy).
\end_layout

